Package: TreeNeighbor
Title: Integration-Free Alignment of Cell-Type Taxonomies Across Resolutions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Michael", "Totty", email = "mictott@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Aligns independently constructed cell-type taxonomies across
    atlases of different resolutions without expression-space integration.
    Implements a MetaNeighbor-derived voting kernel with an exact vote-cache
    additivity property, refinement-invariant tree-intrinsic marginals, and
    the frozen hierarchical walk estimator (votes navigate, AUROC contrasts
    decide) validated on the Allen whole-mouse-brain PL-ILA-ORB benchmark.
    Companion to the primary 'treeneighbor' python package, with which it is
    bit-comparable via a shared portable bootstrap stream. The FUGW transport
    estimator lives in the python package only.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: Matrix, matrixStats, stats
Suggests: testthat
RoxygenNote: 7.3.0
